cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, please cite the associated paper. Author and venue
  metadata are redacted during double-blind review and will be filled in on
  acceptance.
title: "TASCP Reproducibility Artifact: Empirical Validation of a Stateful Moving-Target Defense for DNN-based NIDS"
abstract: >-
  Artifact for the paper evaluating whether a momentum-conditioned Givens
  rotation of the constraint manifold (TASCP) can prevent iterative white-box
  adversaries from crafting adversarial examples against deep network
  intrusion detectors. The artifact contains the defense and attack
  implementations, trained checkpoints, dataset preprocessing, archived
  result records, and verification tooling to reproduce every table and
  figure of the paper.
authors:
  - name: "Anonymous Authors"
    affiliation: "Redacted for double-blind review"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-10-08
license: MIT
keywords:
  - adversarial machine learning
  - network intrusion detection
  - gradient masking
  - moving target defense
  - reproducibility
